NNAAMMEE
     iifflliibb — Network Interface Driver Framework

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     iifflliibb is a framework for writing network interface drivers for FreeBSD.
     It is designed to remove a large amount of the boilerplate that is often
     needed for modern network interface devices, allowing driver authors to
     focus on the specific code needed for their hardware.

     There are three logical components to iifflliibb each of which is described in
     its own manual page.  These are:

     iflibdi(9)    Device-independent functions, used to integrate iifflliibb into
                   the rest of the FreeBSD networking stack.

     iflibdd(9)    Device-dependent functions, used when writing new iifflliibb
                   based drivers.

     iflibtxrx(9)  Device-dependent transmit and receive functions, used when
                   writing new iifflliibb based drivers.

